Falsifies `virtio::verification::a_header_carrying_its_checksum_sums_to_zero`.

The defect: the folded sum loses its complement, `sum as u16` in place of `!(sum as u16)`. The
function still folds the carries and returns a plausible sixteen-bit word, so the line reads as
correct at a glance, but every header the driver sends carries a checksum a receiver rejects.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(ip_checksum(&header), 0)`, for nearly any header.

diff --git a/crates/virtio/src/lib.rs b/crates/virtio/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/virtio/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/virtio/src/lib.rs
@@ -819,3 +819,3 @@ fn ip_checksum(header: &[u8]) -> u16 {
     }
-    !(sum as u16)
+    sum as u16
 }
